parts.text:
Now I'll build the broadcast modernization. Plan:

1. **Breaking ticker component** (`src/components/ticker.tsx`): A full-width broadcast crawl bar at the very top of the page (above hero). "BREAKING" label (amber, pulsing) + scrolling headlines. CSS marquee animation with reduced-motion fallback. Headlines link to articles. Also duplicates content for a seamless loop (aria-hidden duplicate).

2. **Live stats strip** (`src/components/stats-strip.tsx` or inline in page): A thin band between hero and latest showing: LIVE FEED dot, N stories, C categories, A authors, T free tools, current time? A "control room" readout. Use mono type. Could be a `signal-band` full-width with circuit background.

3. **Hero polish**:
   - Add "LIVE" chip on featured card.
   - Update the "last updated" line.

4. Update homepage page.tsx to compose: Ticker → Hero → Stats strip → Latest → ad → Trending → divider → category previews → newsletter → ad.

Let me keep changes tight and reusable. Add the ticker animation CSS to globals.css.

For tools count: getAffiliateCatalog is for affiliate products. Tools pages are static route pages. There are 3 tools (character-counter, meta-description-generator, word-counter). I could hardcode the tools count as 3, but better to avoid magic numbers. The stats strip could show: articles count, categories count, authors count, and "3 free tools". Hmm, hardcoding tools = 3 is fragile but acceptable... Actually let me just show: STORIES (articles), CATEGORIES, AUTHORS, plus "FREE TOOLS" from a constant. There's no exported tools list. I'll hardcode a small constant TOOL_COUNT = 3 with a comment? No comments allowed. Alternatively show "THE SIGNAL · DAILY BRIEFING". 

Let me design the stats strip content from real data: articles, categories, authors. And a "last updated" timestamp from the latest article publishedAt. Four cells. Clean and data-driven.

Now the ticker: to build it I need headlines — latest articles (top ~6). Duplicate for loop. Marquee animation:

```css
@keyframes ticker-scroll {
  from { transform: translateX(0); }
  to { transform: translateX(-50%); }
}
.ticker-track {
  animation: ticker-scroll 40s linear infinite;
  will-change: transform;
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .ticker-track { animation: none; }
}
```

The track contains two identical groups side by side; translating -50% loops seamlessly.

Ticker markup:
```tsx
<aside className="ticker-wrap relative flex items-center gap-4 overflow-hidden border-b border-line bg-surface-2">
  <span className="flex-none px-3 ... bg-amber text-black">BREAKING</span>
  <div className="overflow-hidden flex-1">
    <div className="ticker-track flex w-max items-center">
      {[...items, ...items].map(...)}
    </div>
  </div>
</aside>
```

Wait — the whole ticker-wrap inside max-w container? A broadcast ticker usually spans full width. The page container is max-w-[1440px] px-4. I'll put the ticker full-bleed (outside container) right at top, after header. Header is separate. Let me make the ticker its own component rendered first in the page fragment, full width.

Actually the page content starts with Hero having pt-6. A ticker above it looks good full-bleed.

Let me write the components.

**ticker.tsx**:
```tsx
import Link from "next/link";
import type { Article } from "@/content/types";

export function Ticker({ articles }: { articles: Article[] }) {
  const items = articles.slice(0, 6);
  const doubled = [...items, ...items];
  return (
    <div className="flex items-stretch overflow-hidden border-b border-line bg-surface-2" role="marquee">
      <span className="relative z-10 flex flex-none items-center gap-2 bg-amber px-3 py-2 font-mono text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-black sm:px-4">
        <span className="status-dot is-breaking" aria-hidden="true" />
        Breaking
      </span>
      <div className="relative flex-1 overflow-hidden">
        <div className="ticker-track flex h-full items-center">
          {doubled.map((a, i) => (
            <Link key={`${a.slug}-${i}`} href={`/${a.category}/${a.slug}`} className="flex h-full flex-none items-center gap-2 whitespace-nowrap px-5 font-mono text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.06em] text-muted transition-colors hover:text-fg">
              <span className="text-amber">●</span>
              <span>{a.title}</span>
            </Link>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

Hmm, `role="marquee"` — the ARIA role "marquee" exists. Good.

Note `status-dot is-breaking` has the amber glow; inside an amber background it's fine — maybe use a black dot? On amber bg, the amber dot is invisible. Let me use a simple text "●" black. Actually simpler: just text "BREAKING" on amber bg, no dot. Keep clean.

**stats strip** — I'll inline in page.tsx as a small section, or make a component `live-stats.tsx`. Let me make it a component for cleanliness:

```tsx
import Link from "next/link";
import type { Article } from "@/content/types";

export function LiveStats({ articles, categories, authors }: { articles: Article[]; categories: number; authors: number }) {
  const lastUpdated = new Date(Math.max(...articles.map(a => +new Date(a.publishedAt)))).toLocaleString("en", { hour: "2-digit", minute: "2-digit", hour12: false });
  const cells = [
    { label: "Stories live", value: String(articles.length).padStart(2, "0") },
    { label: "Categories", value: String(categories).padStart(2, "0") },
    { label: "Desk authors", value: String(authors).padStart(2, "0") },
    { label: "Signal feed", value: "24/7" },
  ];
  return (
    <section className="mx-auto max-w-[1440px] px-4">
      <div className="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line bg-line sm:grid-cols-4">
        {cells.map(...)}
      </div>
    </section>
  );
}
```

Using `gap-px bg-line` creates hairline dividers (bg-line is the line color, cells are bg-surface). Nice broadcast dashboard look.

Header cell on the left: "LIVE FEED" with status-dot + "Last update HH:MM". Actually put last-update as part of first cell sub.

Let me refine cells:
- LIVE FEED (with pulsing dot) — value "24/7 · updated HH:MM" 
- Stories: count
- Categories: count
- Authors: count

Grid 2 cols mobile, 4 desktop.

**hero.tsx additions**:
- Add a "LIVE" chip in top-left next to StatusTag? Currently StatusTag is top-left. Add a small "● LIVE FEED" mono label at top-right? The sponsored label occupies top-right when sponsored. Let me add a subtle LIVE chip: actually StatusTag already shows e.g. "BREAKING"/"UPDATED"/"TRENDING". For featured article, tag may exist. Let me check status-tag for kinds. Featured tag likely "breaking" or similar. Adding another "LIVE" chip is redundant. 

Instead, add a "LIVE" indicator + clock line in the meta row: prefix the meta row with a live dot + "LIVE". Let me update the meta row: add `<span className="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-amber"><span className="status-dot is-live" /> Live</span>` before category chip.

Also update hero to accept and pass lastUpdated? Not needed.

Let me now also make the "Read the story" CTA more prominent — it's fine.

Now CSS additions to globals.css:
```css
/* ---------- broadcast ticker ---------- */
