Now the user clarifies: "искам да направиш така да ги напишеш с големи букви всички и другото което не се събира има като more и да се отварят всички категории"

Translation: "I want you to write them all in big letters, and the rest that don't fit should be under 'More', and all categories should open [their pages]."

So: In the header, write the categories with big letters (uppercase, big). Those that don't fit should go into a "More" dropdown/menu. All categories clickable → their category pages.

So redesign the header category nav:
- Show as many categories as fit with big uppercase text links (font-display, bold, uppercase).
- Put the remaining ones in a "More" dropdown (with the rest of the categories, all clickable).

Which categories to show vs More? "другото което не се събира" — the ones that don't fit. I can decide: show first ~6 categories in the bar, put the last 2 (or whatever overflows) into "More". But "don't fit" depends on viewport. A robust approach: use CSS overflow + a "More" that appears when items overflow. That's complex (needs JS measurement). Simpler: show a fixed subset (e.g., first 6: Windows, macOS, Hardware, Software, Internet, Security) as big links, and put the rest (Coding, AI & Automation, plus the utility links All Tutorials/Most Popular/News) in a "More" dropdown.

Actually the user says "всички и другото което не се събира има като more и да се отварят всички категории" = "all [of them] and what doesn't fit should be in More, and all categories should open [when clicked]".

So implement a dropdown "More" containing the categories that don't fit. Let me implement a client component for the dropdown (useState for open/close). The header is a server component; I can create a small client component "MoreMenu" that takes the list of items.

Design decision:
